Source: b1nix-kernel
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: b1nix maintainers <maintainers@b1nix.invalid>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/B1nix/b1nix
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: b1nix-kernel-@RELEASE@
Architecture: @DEB_ARCH@
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, initramfs-tools | initramfs-tools-core
Recommends: limine
Provides: linux-image
Description: Unix-like kernel with the Linux ABI, release @RELEASE@
 The b1nix kernel: a Unix-like monolithic kernel written from scratch that
 implements the Linux system-call ABI, so a stock Debian userspace runs on it
 unmodified.
 .
 This package installs one kernel release. Installing a newer one does not
 remove this one: b1nix keeps the previous kernel and offers it in the boot
 menu, and falls back to it automatically after three failed boots.

Package: b1nix-kernel-@RELEASE@-dbg
Section: debug
Architecture: @DEB_ARCH@
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, b1nix-kernel-@RELEASE@ (= ${binary:Version})
Description: debugging symbols for kernel release @RELEASE@
 The unstripped kernel, indexed by build id, so that a panic captured on a
 machine running the stripped kernel resolves to functions and lines.
 .
 Not needed to run b1nix. Install it when reporting or investigating a crash.

Package: b1nix-kernel-headers-@RELEASE@
Section: devel
Architecture: @DEB_ARCH@
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: module build headers for kernel release @RELEASE@
 The headers and build files needed to compile a module against this kernel
 release.
 .
 These are shipped so that out-of-tree modules can be built. They are not a
 promise that any particular out-of-tree module works: DKMS packages from
 Debian are not supported.

Package: b1nix-kernel
Architecture: @DEB_ARCH@
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, b1nix-kernel-@RELEASE@ (= ${binary:Version})
Description: b1nix kernel (metapackage)
 Depends on the current b1nix kernel release. Upgrading this package pulls in
 the newer kernel while leaving the previous one installed and bootable.
